<.legal_page id="terms" title="Terms of Service" flash={@flash} current_user={@current_user}>
  <p>
    These terms govern your use of the hosted Reviews service at <strong>reviews.figitaki.dev</strong>, including its website, API, CLI sign-in and MCP
    endpoint (together, "the Service"). The Service is operated by <.operator /> ("we", "us").
    By signing in or otherwise using the Service, you agree to these terms. If you use it for an
    organization, you agree for that organization and confirm you may do so.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Reviews source code is licensed separately under the MIT license. These terms cover the
    hosted Service, not your use of the code.
  </p>

  <section id="terms-account">
    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>
      You sign in with a GitHub account and must be at least 13, or older where your local law
      requires. You are responsible for what happens under your account, including everything
      done by agent identities, API tokens, CLI sign-ins and apps you connect. Keep tokens
      secret, and revoke any you no longer use or think may be exposed.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-agents">
    <h2>Agents and connected apps</h2>
    <p>
      You can let AI agents and other tools act on Reviews as an agent identity you own. You are
      responsible for their actions as if they were your own, and for choosing which apps to
      trust. Apps you connect, such as Claude, ChatGPT or Amp, are provided by others under their
      own terms; we do not control them and are not responsible for them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-content">
    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <p>
      You keep ownership of the diffs, review packets, comments and other content you or your
      agents submit ("your content"). You give us a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free
      license to host, store, copy, process and display your content only as needed to run,
      secure and improve the Service, and to show it to anyone who has its link.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Reviews are shared by link.</strong>
      Anyone with a review's URL can read it and its comments without signing in. Do not submit
      secrets, credentials, personal information about others, or code you do not have the
      right to share. You confirm you have the rights needed to submit your content.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-acceptable-use">
    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        break the law or infringe anyone's rights, including by uploading code you may not share;
      </li>
      <li>upload malware, or content meant to harass, deceive or harm others;</li>
      <li>
        try to get around rate limits, access controls or authentication, or access data that is not yours;
      </li>
      <li>
        overload, disrupt or probe the Service, except through a coordinated security report;
      </li>
      <li>use the Service as general file hosting, or resell it without our permission;</li>
      <li>
        impersonate a person, organization or app, including through an agent identity's name.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Automated use through the CLI, the API and MCP is expected, within the rate limits and
      these rules.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-removal">
    <h2>Removal and suspension</h2>
    <p>
      We may remove content, revoke tokens or app connections, or suspend or close accounts that
      break these terms or put the Service or others at risk. Where it is practical and
      lawful, we will tell you why. You can stop using the Service at any time and ask us to
      delete your account by emailing <.contact />.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-service">
    <h2>Changes to the Service</h2>
    <p>
      Reviews is a small, evolving tool. We may add, change or remove features, change limits,
      or stop offering the Service. If we plan to shut it down, we will try to give reasonable
      notice so you can save your content. The Service is free today; if we introduce paid
      features, we will tell you before you are charged.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-privacy">
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href={~p"/privacy"}>Privacy Policy</a> explains what we collect and how we use it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-feedback">
    <h2>Feedback</h2>
    <p>
      If you send us ideas or feedback, we may use them without obligation to you.
      Contributions to the source code are covered by the repository's license instead.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-warranty">
    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is provided <strong>"as is" and "as available"</strong>, without warranties of
      any kind, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose
      and non-infringement. We do not promise that it will be uninterrupted, secure or free of
      errors, or that content will never be lost. Keep your own copies of anything important.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-liability">
    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special,
      consequential or punitive damages, or for lost profits, data or goodwill, arising from your
      use of the Service. Our total liability for any claim about the Service is limited to the
      greater of the amount you paid us for it in the 12 months before the claim and <.placeholder>[LIABILITY CAP, e.g. US$100]</.placeholder>. Some places do not allow these
      limits, so they may not apply to you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-indemnity">
    <h2>Indemnity</h2>
    <p>
      You agree to cover our reasonable costs from claims by others that arise from your content,
      your agents' actions, or your breach of these terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-law">
    <h2>Governing law and disputes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of <.placeholder>[GOVERNING LAW]</.placeholder>, without
      regard to conflict-of-law rules. Disputes will be resolved in the courts of <.placeholder>[VENUE]</.placeholder>, unless the law where you live gives you the right to
      bring them elsewhere.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-changes">
    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. We will change the date at the top, and for significant changes
      give notice on the site or by email before they take effect. Using the Service after that
      means you accept the new terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-general">
    <h2>General</h2>
    <p>
      These terms and the Privacy Policy are the whole agreement between you and us about the
      Service. If a part is found unenforceable, the rest still applies. Not enforcing a term is
      not a waiver of it. You may not transfer these terms without our consent; we may transfer
      them to whoever takes over the Service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-contact">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms: <.contact />, <.operator />.</p>
  </section>
</.legal_page>
